// Individually edited scenarios, repair decisions and quote factors for existing services.
// No new service URLs, price amounts, qualifications or project claims are introduced.
module.exports = {
 'air-conditioning': ['Weak cooling, water drips or noisy operation', 'Tell Ellis whether one room or the whole home is affected and whether the fault is intermittent. We check the system and the affected areas so a service visit addresses the cause, not only the visible symptom.', 'Repair the existing unit or plan a replacement?', 'A repair assessment considers the equipment condition, fault and compatible parts. A replacement also involves room layout, indoor and outdoor locations and electrical requirements. We explain the proposed work before you choose an option.', 'System type, number of units, access, fault investigation, compatible parts and installation requirements affect the quote.', ['electricians','insulation']],
 'blinds-and-curtains': ['Sagging curtain rods and loose blind brackets', 'A bracket pulling away from the wall needs the fixing surface checked, not simply another screw in the same damaged hole. Ellis assesses the bracket, rod span and wall material before agreeing the repair.', 'Fitting new curtains or replacing damaged blinds', 'We check the opening, product dimensions and mounting clearances. Supplied blinds need compatible fittings and enough space to operate. Electrical work for powered products is separated from ordinary rod or bracket installation.', 'The number of openings, product type, fitting surface, replacement hardware and access affect the installation or repair price.', ['handymen','electricians']],
 'carpenters': ['Damaged trim after flooring or a furniture move', 'Loose skirting, chipped architraves and damaged door trim can often be assessed as a grouped repair. Ellis checks the profile and surrounding surface so replacement sections fit the agreed finish rather than stand out unnecessarily.', 'Local timber repair or a larger replacement?', 'We examine how much sound timber remains and whether moisture or movement caused the damage. A trim repair differs from replacing a frame or altering load-bearing timber. The quote identifies preparation, fitting and any finishing work.', 'Timber profile and availability, damaged length, access, joinery detail and painting or staining requirements affect the quote.', ['handymen','house-painters']],
 'carpet-repair': ['A burn, tear or damaged patch in one room', 'Ellis checks the damaged area, carpet construction and any matching offcut you have. A patch needs a suitable piece and a stable surrounding carpet. We explain the likely appearance before you approve the work.', 'Loose edges and wrinkles near a doorway', 'A lifting join or wrinkle may involve the fixing, underlay or carpet tension. We assess these together rather than hide the edge with a trim. Wider wear or unavailable matching carpet may make replacement worth comparing.', 'Patch size, matching material, seam location, underlay condition and furniture movement affect repair costs.', ['new-carpet','removalists']],
 'cladding': ['Cracked panels, loose boards or water around openings', 'Tell Ellis where the exterior cladding is damaged and whether water appears inside after rain. We inspect the affected area and surrounding junctions before deciding whether the job is a panel repair or a wider weatherproofing issue.', 'Replacing a section without hiding the cause', 'Local replacement depends on the remaining support, compatible material and condition behind the cladding. Older unknown materials need assessment before disturbance. We confirm the repair, preparation and finishing as separate parts of the scope.', 'Cladding type, panel availability, height, underlying damage and finishing or flashing work influence the quote.', ['window-repairs','roofing']],
 'electricians': ['Tripping circuits, faulty lights or damaged power points', 'Describe what stopped working and when it happens. Ellis arranges the electrical assessment so the fault can be investigated rather than assuming a new fitting will fix it. Fixed electrical work is handled under the applicable licensing requirements.', 'Adding lighting or power during a renovation', 'Bring the proposed room layout and appliance locations. We review fitting positions, existing circuits and access before agreeing changes. Surface fitting replacement, new wiring and switchboard work are different scopes and should be itemised accordingly.', 'Fault-finding time, circuit changes, fittings, wiring access and switchboard requirements affect the electrical quote.', ['plumbers','air-conditioning']],
 'floor-sanding': ['Worn coatings, scratches and uneven colour', 'Ellis assesses the timber, existing finish and remaining condition before recommending sanding and recoating. Scratches in a coating and damage in the timber may need different preparation; not every floor is suitable for another sanding.', 'Repairing boards before finishing the surface', 'Loose boards, moisture marks or movement need attention before the new coating is applied. We agree any board repairs, room preparation and finish selection with you. Access while the finish dries is planned for an occupied property.', 'Floor area, coating removal, edge detail, board repairs, furniture clearance and the selected finish affect pricing.', ['carpenters','removalists']],
 'fly-screens': ['Torn mesh on several windows or screen doors', 'List the openings with damaged mesh and tell Ellis if any frames no longer sit properly. We assess which frames can be retained, the compatible mesh and the fittings, so remeshing is not quoted as a complete screen replacement.', 'A dragging screen door or a heavy glass panel', 'Mesh work, frame adjustment and rollers are distinct repairs. We identify which panel is causing the problem. Glass sliding door rollers and track repairs are also available through our handyman service, with the panel handling requirements checked.', 'Screen quantity, opening size, mesh choice, reusable frames and replacement hardware determine the work and quote.', ['handymen','window-repairs']],
 'insulation': ['Cold rooms or uneven insulation coverage', 'Tell Ellis which areas are uncomfortable and what you know about the existing insulation. We assess accessible coverage and condition before recommending filling gaps or a broader upgrade. A comfort complaint alone does not establish the required material.', 'Planning ceiling, wall or underfloor work', 'Different parts of a home have different access and moisture considerations. The installation plan identifies the areas included and any preparation needed. You do not need to enter a roof space or subfloor to prepare the enquiry.', 'The area, construction, access, existing material removal and selected insulation system affect the quote.', ['air-conditioning','roofing']],
 'new-carpet': ['Replacing worn carpet in bedrooms or living areas', 'Ellis checks the rooms, existing covering, underlay and floor condition before agreeing a new carpet installation. Include furniture, stairs and thresholds in the brief so the quote reflects the actual fitting work.', 'Repair one area or replace the room carpet?', 'A small damaged patch may be repairable when matching carpet is available. Extensive wear, repeated damage or a new room finish may call for replacement. We distinguish lifting old carpet, floor preparation and fitting the new product.', 'Carpet and underlay selection, room shape, stairs, removal, disposal and furniture clearance affect the price.', ['carpet-repair','handymen']],
 'plasterers': ['Wall holes, damaged corners and removed fittings', 'Tell Ellis which rooms need wall patching and whether the damage came from an impact or removed fixture. We inspect the edges and supporting material before repairing the patch, rather than fill over a weak area.', 'Ceiling patches, cornice damage and finishing', 'Recurring cracks, sagging or water marks need the underlying condition checked before cosmetic work. For suitable repairs, we agree patching and the finish required. Painting a patch or repainting a whole wall is a separate choice in the quote.', 'Patch size, wall or ceiling access, cornice profile, preparation and the agreed paint finish influence the quote.', ['house-painters','roofing']],
 'plumbers': ['Leaks, overflowing fixtures and blocked sinks', 'Tell Ellis which fixtures are affected and where water appears. We arrange the plumbing assessment to distinguish a local fixture fault from a pipe or drainage problem. The agreed repair follows the findings, rather than a presumed cause.', 'Replacing a tap or investigating a shower leak', 'Replacing a fixture and altering pipework are different jobs. Shower water may come from plumbing or the tiled wet area. We identify the work needed and separate plumbing, surface sealing and waterproofing where more than one service is involved.', 'The fault location, fixture selection, access to pipework, clearing work and making good affect the plumbing quote.', ['waterproofing','tiling']],
 'shower-screens': ['A shower door that catches or water escapes at its edge', 'Ellis checks the door operation, fittings and visible seals. A worn screen seal and a leak through the wet-area construction are different issues. We assess where water appears before agreeing a hardware or sealing repair.', 'Replacing the screen without guessing the fit', 'We measure the opening and check the existing tiles, clearances and attachment points. A new screen quote identifies product supply, removal and installation. Damage to glass or supporting surfaces requires the appropriate assessment before handling.', 'Screen size and design, glass and fittings, removal, tile condition and access affect the replacement quote.', ['glass-glaziers','waterproofing']],
 'tiling': ['Cracked kitchen tiles or loose flooring', 'We inspect the affected tile and supporting surface before proposing a local replacement. Matching spare tiles help, but repeated cracking or loosening may indicate a substrate problem. Ellis explains the repair area and any underlying work required.', 'Missing grout or a shower that still leaks', 'Renewing grout or silicone is surface maintenance, not replacement of the waterproofing beneath tiles. Persistent damp areas need assessment before another cosmetic repair. The quote distinguishes local tile work, regrouting and any deeper wet-area investigation.', 'Tile availability, repair area, removal, substrate condition, grout choice and waterproofing requirements affect the quote.', ['waterproofing','handymen']],
 'waterproofing': ['A shower leak that returns after resealing', 'A renewed silicone joint may not resolve damage beneath the tiles. Ellis assesses the affected wet area and visible water damage before agreeing investigation or repair. Tell us what was previously repaired and whether the leak changed.', 'Waterproofing during bathroom or balcony repairs', 'The plan distinguishes surface maintenance from work involving tile removal, the substrate and a waterproofing system. We agree what must be exposed and reinstated before work proceeds. Plumbing faults and damaged finishes are identified separately.', 'Access, investigation, tile removal, substrate repairs, waterproofing area and reinstatement determine the quoted scope.', ['bathroom','tiling']],
 'asbestos-removal': ['Older sheets, damaged fencing or unknown building material', 'Tell Ellis where the material is and what work is planned. Unknown old sheets should be assessed before drilling, cutting or removal. We arrange the appropriate assessment and confirm the required removal scope rather than diagnose material from a photograph.', 'Separating removal from the replacement work', 'Material identification, access, removal arrangements and disposal need to be confirmed before the site is disturbed. Replacement fencing, cladding or finishes are distinct work items. The quote makes clear which activities and follow-on repairs are included.', 'Material type and quantity, condition, access, required controls and disposal arrangements affect the removal quote.', ['fence-builders','cladding']],
 'concrete-resurfacing': ['A worn driveway, path or outdoor concrete finish', 'Ellis assesses the existing slab and surface before recommending resurfacing. The work addresses a suitable surface, not a promise to correct every crack or movement problem. Describe peeling coatings, worn areas and any pooling water.', 'Surface refresh or repair the slab first?', 'Cracks, lifting or ongoing moisture may need investigation before a new finish is applied. We agree any repairs and preparation separately from the chosen coating. Different traffic and exposure conditions affect the suitable finish.', 'Area, coating removal, slab repairs, access, preparation and finish selection affect the resurfacing price.', ['concreters','pavers']],
 'gutter-services': ['Blocked outlets, overflow and leaking gutter joints', 'Ellis checks debris, outlets, downpipes and the affected joints. Cleaning removes accessible build-up, while leaks or poor drainage may need repair as well. Tell us where overflow occurs so the assessment covers the full drainage problem.', 'Loose brackets, rust or damaged gutter sections', 'Sound guttering may suit a local bracket or joint repair. Widespread corrosion, damaged falls or deteriorated downpipes may call for replacement. We separate clearing, repairs and replacement components in the quote so you can approve the actual work.', 'Gutter length, building height, safe access, debris removal, replacement parts and downpipe condition affect the quote.', ['roofing','rubbish-removal']],
 'house-painters': ['Touch-ups after repairs or a room repaint', 'Tell Ellis whether you want patched walls, door trim or an entire room painted. We assess the existing coating and required finish. A touch-up on aged paint may remain visible, so the repair area and blending expectations are agreed first.', 'Peeling exterior paint or damp surfaces', 'Preparation depends on the condition, not only the colour choice. Loose coatings and recurring moisture need assessment before repainting. We identify cleaning, filling, sanding and any prior repair work in the scope, together with the paint system.', 'Surface area, preparation, access, coating condition, product selection and coats required influence the painting quote.', ['plasterers','carpenters']],
 'door-installation': ['A new internal door in an existing opening', 'Ellis measures the opening and checks the frame, swing and clearance. Fitting a door to an existing frame may involve trimming and compatible hinges or handles. Product supply and final painting are agreed rather than assumed.', 'A rubbing door may need repair instead', 'An existing door that catches can involve hinges, alignment or a changed floor height. We assess whether an adjustment is suitable before replacing it. External, glazed, security and fire-rated doors have product-specific requirements and are not treated as ordinary internal doors.', 'Door type, frame condition, hardware, trimming, removal and finishing affect the installation quote.', ['handymen','carpenters']],
 'pavers': ['Sunken pavers, raised edges or pooling water', 'Ellis inspects the affected paving and support underneath before agreeing a repair. Lifting and relaying pavers may need base or drainage work as well. Simply filling a visible gap does not correct continuing ground movement.', 'Adding a path or extending a paved area', 'We check levels, edges, access and the connection to existing surfaces. The plan identifies excavation, base preparation and the paving material. Matching an older product depends on availability, so the intended appearance is discussed before ordering.', 'Area, excavation, base repairs, drainage, edging and paver supply determine the price.', ['concreters','garden-landscapers']],
 'roofing': ['Rainwater entering or damaged roof coverings', 'Tell Ellis where water appears inside and whether it occurs after particular weather. We arrange a safe roof assessment to check the affected covering and junctions. An interior stain does not by itself identify the roof repair needed.', 'A local roof repair or a wider replacement?', 'Individual damaged tiles or sheets may suit local repair where the surrounding roof remains suitable. Recurring leaks or deteriorated materials may need a broader scope. We identify the repair area and related gutter or flashing work before quoting.', 'Roof type, affected area, safe access, compatible materials and any junction or drainage repairs influence the quote.', ['gutter-services','plasterers']],
 'skylights': ['A dark room or a leaking existing skylight', 'For a new skylight, Ellis checks the roof and ceiling arrangement and the position you want to brighten. For a leak, we assess the skylight and surrounding junctions before deciding whether repair or replacement is appropriate.', 'Product replacement and changes inside the room', 'The quote distinguishes roof work, the skylight product and any internal lining or finishing. An existing opening is checked rather than assumed to fit a new model. Powered blinds or electrical components require their own electrical scope.', 'Product type, roof access, opening changes, internal lining and electrical requirements affect the skylight quote.', ['roofing','electricians']],
 'verandah-builders': ['Weathered boards or a damaged verandah section', 'Ellis checks the affected boards, roof elements and supports before agreeing repairs. A visible damaged finish may not be the only problem. Tell us about movement or water entry so the repair does not conceal deterioration.', 'Planning an addition attached to the home', 'We assess the layout, connection to the existing building and the proposed materials. Structural and approval requirements are checked before the scope is agreed. A new verandah and repairing retained components need different plans and quotes.', 'Size, foundations, building connections, roof materials, access and documentation requirements affect the price.', ['deck-builders','structural-engineers']],
 'window-installation': ['Replacing an old window within the existing opening', 'Ellis measures the opening and checks the frame, surrounding finish and access. We discuss the replacement product and how it will operate. Removing the old unit, fitting and making good are identified in the installation scope.', 'Repair the frame or replace the whole window?', 'A sticking sash or worn fitting may be a repair job rather than a complete replacement. Rot, widespread damage or a different product design may change the recommendation. Glass, hardware and frame work are assessed separately.', 'Window size and type, glazing, height, opening preparation and internal or external finishing affect the quote.', ['window-repairs','glass-glaziers']],
 'window-repairs': ['Sticking sashes, loose handles or worn hinges', 'Ellis checks the window movement and compatible hardware before agreeing adjustment or replacement parts. Tell us whether it catches when opening, closing or latching. Several faulty windows can be assessed together as one repair list.', 'Rotten sills or moisture around the frame', 'We inspect the affected timber and surrounding area to see whether a local repair is suitable. Painting over soft timber does not address its cause. Broken glass and a complete window replacement are distinct scopes, with their own requirements.', 'Frame condition, repair size, compatible hardware, access and finishing requirements affect the repair price.', ['carpenters','window-installation']],
 'deck-builders': ['Loose boards, splinters or damaged decking sections', 'Ellis checks the affected boards and accessible support before agreeing a replacement. The condition beneath the surface matters. We identify board repair, fixing work and any structural investigation separately rather than assume a new coating will resolve instability.', 'Refinishing the deck or building a new one', 'Surface maintenance depends on the timber and existing coating. A new deck also involves layout, supports and construction requirements. We confirm the retained structure and the work included so maintenance and new construction are not mixed in one vague brief.', 'Deck area, timber choice, supports, board replacement, preparation and finishing affect the quote.', ['carpenters','verandah-builders']],
 'fence-builders': ['A damaged fence panel or a failing post', 'Ellis checks the panel, posts and adjacent sections before agreeing local replacement. Damage that looks limited to a panel can involve the support. We identify retained components and replacement materials before the work is approved.', 'Replacing a boundary fence', 'Tell us which sections are included and who approves the boundary work. The existing fence position is not treated as a survey. A new layout may need boundary confirmation, access planning and checks for adjoining structures.', 'Fence length, height, material, post work, removal, disposal and access influence the quote.', ['timber-fencing','surveyors']],
 'fencing-contractors': ['A fence project with several sections and gates', 'List the boundary runs, screening areas and gate locations you want included. Ellis assesses supports, levels and access so the plan covers more than the visible panels. Gate clearances and the intended use are checked with the layout.', 'Different requirements at pools and retaining walls', 'An ordinary garden fence is not the same job as a pool barrier or a fence supported near a retaining wall. We identify the applicable design and support requirements before agreeing materials or changes. Repairs and full replacement are itemised separately.', 'Fence specification, gates, ground conditions, supports, demolition and access determine the quoted scope.', ['pool-fence-installers','retaining-walls']],
 'garden-clean-up': ['An overgrown yard before an inspection or move', 'Ellis assesses weeding, cutbacks, fallen material and the green waste to remove. Identify plants you want retained and areas that must stay accessible. The task list distinguishes tidying from new landscaping or substantial tree work.', 'Combining garden work with outdoor repairs', 'A clean-up can be planned with suitable pressure cleaning or small handyman repairs. Declare old building debris or suspect hazardous material before work. We agree the waste types and collection arrangements rather than assume everything in the yard is green waste.', 'Garden size, growth, access, green-waste volume and the agreed additional tasks affect the quote.', ['handymen','rubbish-removal']],
 'garden-landscapers': ['Refreshing garden beds and worn edging', 'Ellis discusses the planting, beds and edges you want retained or changed. The assessment considers the existing garden and access before agreeing materials and preparation. A small bed refresh and a full redesign have different scopes.', 'Changing levels or adding a path', 'Ground levels, water flow and adjoining structures need consideration before landscaping begins. We separate planting work from retaining walls, paving or drainage changes. The proposed layout makes clear which elements are included in the quote.', 'Plant and material selection, area, soil preparation, access and built garden features affect pricing.', ['pavers','retaining-walls']],
 'gardeners': ['Routine weeding, pruning and mulch', 'Tell Ellis which beds need attention and which plants you want kept. We agree a task list for the visit so gardening does not mean an undefined whole-yard makeover. Mulch supply and green-waste handling are included only as agreed.', 'A one-off tidy or ongoing maintenance', 'A neglected garden may need an initial clean-up before routine visits are practical. We distinguish reachable garden pruning from arborist work on substantial trees. Frequency and seasonal tasks can be discussed after the garden condition is assessed.', 'Bed size, plant density, pruning scope, mulch and waste handling affect the maintenance quote.', ['garden-clean-up','tree-arborists']],
 'lawn-mowing': ['Long grass and overgrown lawn edges', 'Ellis checks the lawn area, grass condition and access before agreeing mowing and edging. Identify obstacles, pets and irrigation fittings you know about. Clipping collection or mulching is confirmed so the result matches the requested clean-up.', 'Mowing versus restoring a damaged lawn', 'Bare patches, uneven ground and persistent wet areas may need work beyond cutting the grass. We distinguish routine mowing from garden repairs or a replacement surface. Tell us if the lawn is part of a move-out or inspection task list.', 'Lawn size, growth, edging length, access and clipping disposal affect the mowing price.', ['gardeners','synthetic-grass']],
 'patio-builders': ['Planning a usable outdoor patio surface', 'Ellis checks the intended area, levels and connection to the home. The plan considers steps, drainage and how you use the outdoor space. Surface work is described separately from an overhead patio roof or cover.', 'Repairing the base or replacing the surface', 'An uneven or failing surface may require preparation underneath, not simply a new finish. We assess the retained base and boundaries before agreeing repairs or installation. Any roof, pergola or structural work needs its own defined scope.', 'Area, ground preparation, surface materials, edges, steps and drainage requirements affect the quote.', ['pavers','pergola-builders']],
 'pergola-builders': ['Weathered timber or a loose pergola component', 'Ellis checks the affected timber, connections and supports before agreeing a local repair. Surface wear and structural deterioration need different work. Describe movement or recurring water damage so the assessment addresses the underlying condition.', 'Repairing an existing pergola or planning a new one', 'We identify components suitable to retain and what needs replacement. A new structure also needs layout, support and approval requirements checked. The scope separates ordinary trim repairs from work on load-bearing posts or beams.', 'Structure size, timber, supports, access, removal and any design requirements affect the pergola quote.', ['handymen','structural-engineers']],
 'pool-fence-installers': ['A pool gate that will not close or latch', 'Tell Ellis about the gate operation and the affected barrier section. Pool gate work needs the relevant safety requirements considered, not only a convenient latch position. Do not assume an ordinary garden-gate repair is suitable for a pool barrier.', 'Replacing a barrier section or changing its layout', 'The assessment checks the proposed materials, connections and surrounding access. We identify installation and any inspection or approval steps needed for the work. A repair should not be described as certification of the whole barrier.', 'Barrier length, gate hardware, fixing surfaces, product requirements and removal affect the quote.', ['fencing-contractors','building-inspectors']],
 'pool-resurfacing': ['A worn finish or visible damage to the pool surface', 'Ellis assesses the existing finish and pool shell before agreeing resurfacing. Peeling, staining and cracks may need different preparation. Tell us about earlier repairs and whether any damage keeps returning.', 'Surface renewal versus repairs to the shell', 'Resurfacing is not automatically a solution for structural cracks or other underlying faults. The plan identifies preparation, any prior repair and the selected finish. Do not drain the pool solely to prepare an enquiry; arrangements are confirmed after assessment.', 'Pool size, existing finish, preparation, shell repairs and site access affect the resurfacing price.', ['structural-engineers','pool-fence-installers']],
 'surveyors': ['Survey information for a fence or renovation', 'Tell Ellis whether you need boundary information, existing features or levels for a design. The intended use determines the survey scope. A measured feature plan is not automatically confirmation of the legal boundary.', 'Preparing the brief for the right survey output', 'Include available plans and the area being changed, if you have them. We agree the deliverable and any access requirements before the work. A fence location, building design and approval process may need different survey information.', 'Survey purpose, site size, access, available records and the required deliverables affect the quote.', ['fence-builders','draftsmen']],
 'synthetic-grass': ['Replacing a difficult lawn or creating a small play area', 'Ellis checks the existing surface and intended use before agreeing synthetic turf. Pets, foot traffic and the surrounding edges affect the layout. Product supply and installation preparation are identified separately in the quote.', 'A stable base and suitable water flow', 'Uneven ground or poor drainage may need base work before the turf is laid. We assess what must be removed and retained so the new surface does not simply hide an existing problem. Edges and joins are planned with the installation.', 'Area, excavation, base preparation, turf specification, edging and access affect the price.', ['garden-landscapers','lawn-mowing']],
 'timber-fencing': ['Broken palings, loose rails or a leaning post', 'Ellis checks the damaged section and adjoining support before agreeing repairs. Individual palings can be replaced where the fence remains suitable. Continuing movement or a deteriorated post may require more than a new panel.', 'A timber side gate that drags or will not latch', 'We assess the hinges, latch, frame and supporting posts together. An adjustment or compatible hardware may suit a sound gate, while damaged timber needs its own repair. Pool gates are a separate safety-related scope.', 'Timber type, repair length, post condition, hardware, removal and access influence the quote.', ['fence-builders','pool-fence-installers']],
 'tree-arborists': ['Damaged branches or concerns about a tree', 'Describe the tree location, visible damage and nearby structures. Ellis arranges the appropriate tree assessment before pruning or removal is agreed. A hanging branch or unstable tree is not treated as routine garden maintenance.', 'Retaining a tree or planning removal', 'The condition, location and proposed result determine the work. We agree the pruning or removal area, access and debris handling. Do not assume stump work or every nearby tree is included in a single enquiry.', 'Tree size and condition, access, nearby structures, equipment and waste handling affect the quote.', ['gardeners','rubbish-removal']],
 'bathroom': ['A shower that leaks after repeated surface repairs', 'Ellis assesses the visible damage and previous work before agreeing the repair. Silicone, grout, pipework and the waterproofing layer are different possible scopes. Replacing a surface joint should not be presented as a complete wet-area repair.', 'Updating fixtures or renovating the whole bathroom', 'Tell us which fixtures and finishes you want retained. The plan identifies removal, plumbing, electrical work, substrate preparation and finishing where required. Occupied-home access and the availability of bathroom facilities need to be discussed before work starts.', 'Room size, retained fixtures, removal, substrate condition, trade work and selected finishes affect the renovation quote.', ['waterproofing','plumbers']],
 'bricklayers': ['Damaged bricks, missing mortar or a broken pier', 'Ellis checks the affected masonry and surrounding condition before agreeing a local repair. Brick and mortar matching depends on the existing material and availability. We discuss the repair boundary and intended appearance before ordering replacements.', 'Cracking or a leaning wall', 'Movement needs assessment rather than another surface patch. The required work may involve support or structural advice before rebuilding. We separate local masonry repair from work on retaining structures or load-bearing elements.', 'Repair size, brick availability, mortar finish, access and any support requirements influence the price.', ['structural-engineers','retaining-walls']],
 'builders': ['A renovation, extension or defined building repair', 'Bring the changes you want and any existing plans to Ellis. We assess the retained building, site access and the proposed work. Small repairs, renovation and new construction are distinguished so the brief is clear before pricing.', 'Agreeing construction and approval responsibilities', 'The scope identifies the design, applicable documentation, required approvals and construction work. We clarify what is included before work proceeds. Discovering an existing defect may change the plan and needs an agreed change, not an assumed extra.', 'Project size, design, structural work, materials, site conditions and documentation affect the building quote.', ['draftsmen','structural-engineers']],
 'building-certifiers': ['Documentation for a building or renovation proposal', 'Tell Ellis which project stage you have reached and what certification or approval documents have been requested. We identify the appropriate documentation scope. Reviewing compliance is distinct from designing the project or carrying out the building work.', 'Clarifying what the document covers', 'Available plans, engineering information and site details help define the work. The agreed deliverable should identify the relevant project and exclusions. A certification enquiry is not a promise that an unassessed proposal will receive approval.', 'Project type, document completeness, review requirements and the agreed deliverables influence the quote.', ['draftsmen','builders']],
 'building-inspectors': ['A pre-purchase, handover or targeted defect inspection', 'Tell Ellis the reason for the inspection and any area of concern. We agree the inspection scope, accessible areas and report before the visit. A targeted defect enquiry and a broader property inspection need different briefs.', 'Understanding the report and following up repairs', 'Inspection findings do not automatically include destructive investigation or every specialist system. The report should distinguish observations and further checks. If repairs are needed, their assessment and quotation are arranged separately from the inspection service.', 'Property size, inspection purpose, access, report scope and specialist follow-up affect the price.', ['structural-engineers','handymen']],
 'carports-and-garages': ['A new vehicle shelter or changes to an existing garage', 'Ellis checks the intended layout, vehicle clearance and connection to the property. Foundations, drainage and building requirements need consideration before the scope is agreed. Product selection alone does not define the complete construction work.', 'Repairing selected components instead of rebuilding', 'Damaged trim or a local component may be repairable where the supporting structure remains suitable. We assess deterioration and movement before agreeing retained elements. Structural repairs and a new build require a different plan from minor maintenance.', 'Structure size, supports, foundations, materials, access and documentation requirements affect pricing.', ['builders','concreters']],
 'concreters': ['A path, outdoor slab or other concrete flatwork', 'Tell Ellis how the area will be used and where it connects to existing surfaces. We assess levels, access and preparation before agreeing the pour. Excavation, formwork and finishing should be part of a defined scope.', 'Repairing a surface or planning structural concrete', 'Worn coatings may suit resurfacing, while a structural slab or footing has different design requirements. We identify the correct scope rather than treat every concrete area as ordinary flatwork. Drainage and existing movement are considered before work.', 'Area, thickness and specification, excavation, reinforcement, access and finish affect the quote.', ['concrete-resurfacing','structural-engineers']],
 'demolition': ['Removing selected rooms, fittings or building elements', 'Ellis confirms exactly what is to be removed and what must remain. Access, occupied areas and existing services affect the plan. A kitchen strip-out and demolition of a structure are different scopes, with different preparation and safety requirements.', 'Material checks and follow-on repairs', 'Older unknown materials and structural components need assessment before disturbance. We identify disconnection, removal and waste arrangements, plus any making good. New construction after demolition is separately agreed rather than implied by the removal quote.', 'Removal area, materials, service disconnections, access, required controls and disposal affect the quote.', ['asbestos-removal','builders']],
 'draftsmen': ['Turning a renovation brief into drawings', 'Tell Ellis the rooms or building changes you want and the purpose of the drawings. Concept layouts and detailed construction documents are not the same deliverable. We clarify the drawing stage before agreeing the work.', 'Coordinating plans with survey and engineering', 'The required documents depend on the proposal and approval process. Existing-site measurements, boundary information and structural design may need separate input. The drafting scope identifies what is included and what information is needed from the other work.', 'Project complexity, drawing stage, existing information, revisions and documentation requirements affect the quote.', ['surveyors','structural-engineers']],
 'home-renovators': ['Updating rooms while retaining parts of the home', 'List what you want changed and what should stay. Ellis checks the existing condition so the renovation plan includes repairs that affect the new work. Cabinet alterations, wet-area work and structural changes are identified rather than bundled without detail.', 'Planning stages in an occupied property', 'Access, dust-sensitive areas and the continued use of rooms affect the work sequence. We discuss stages and dependencies before agreeing the plan. Known leaks or movement need assessment rather than being covered by new finishes.', 'Rooms included, removal, retained fixtures, trade work, materials and staging requirements influence the quote.', ['builders','bathroom']],
 'renderers': ['Chipped render or a damaged wall section', 'Ellis checks the affected area and surrounding surface before agreeing a local render repair. The existing texture and coating influence preparation. We discuss finish matching and any repainting rather than assume a patch will disappear.', 'Recurring cracks or damp beneath the finish', 'Render is a surface finish, not a cure for continuing movement or water entry. The cause needs assessment before new material is applied. The scope identifies preparation, repair and finishing, with further investigation if the wall condition requires it.', 'Repair area, texture, substrate condition, access and paint finish affect the rendering quote.', ['bricklayers','house-painters']],
 'restumping': ['Uneven floors or concerns about underfloor supports', 'Tell Ellis where movement is noticed and whether it has changed. An uneven floor alone does not establish that the home needs restumping. We arrange assessment of the supports and surrounding condition before proposing work.', 'Support repair versus a wider restumping project', 'The plan identifies affected supports, access and any structural requirements. Local deterioration and broader movement can require different solutions. You do not need to enter a difficult subfloor to prepare the enquiry; describe the symptoms you have noticed.', 'Number and condition of supports, subfloor access, structural requirements and the agreed repair area affect pricing.', ['structural-engineers','carpenters']],
 'retaining-walls': ['A leaning wall, displaced blocks or drainage concerns', 'Ellis checks the visible condition, retained ground and nearby structures before agreeing repair or replacement. The ground pressure and water conditions matter. Simply matching the old wall does not establish that the same design remains suitable.', 'Planning a replacement or a new garden level', 'Wall height, position and load affect the required design and approval checks. We identify excavation, supports and drainage in the scope. Landscaping and boundary fencing are considered separately where they depend on the retaining wall.', 'Wall dimensions, material, ground conditions, drainage, access and design requirements affect the quote.', ['structural-engineers','garden-landscapers']],
 'structural-engineers': ['Cracks, movement or an alteration involving supports', 'Tell Ellis what has changed and provide existing plans if available. The assessment considers the affected structure, not only the visible crack. We define the engineering advice or design needed before a building repair is agreed.', 'Removing a wall or changing a beam', 'The load-bearing role and surrounding structure need to be assessed before alteration. Engineering documentation and construction are different deliverables. The scope identifies the proposed change, required checks and information for the building work.', 'Assessment purpose, structure type, available drawings, investigation and design deliverables affect the engineering quote.', ['builders','draftsmen']],
 'cabinet-makers': ['Fitted storage or a change to the kitchen layout', 'Ellis checks the dimensions, retained cabinets and intended use before agreeing new cabinetry or alterations. Doors, drawers and appliance openings are planned together. The design identifies materials and hardware so supply and fitting have a clear scope.', 'A dropped cupboard door may only need repair', 'Loose hinges, drawer runners and alignment faults are also covered by our handyman repair service. We distinguish hardware repairs from replacing cabinet carcasses or making new storage. Appliance connections are a separate trade requirement, not part of cabinetry alone.', 'Cabinet quantity, materials, hardware, appliance openings, removal and fitting details affect the quote.', ['handymen','ikea-kitchens']],
 'cleaners': ['A home clean or an end-of-lease task list', 'Tell Ellis the rooms and tasks you want included, including cupboards or appliances where relevant. We agree the condition and work list before pricing. An end-of-lease clean is a defined service, not a guarantee of an inspection or bond result.', 'Cleaning after building work or an outdoor tidy', 'Ordinary dust and cleaning tasks differ from hazardous residues or specialist material removal. Declare the site condition before booking. Outdoor pressure cleaning is also available through our handyman service, with the surface and runoff assessed separately.', 'Property size, condition, included tasks, access and any separately agreed specialist work affect the cleaning quote.', ['handymen','rubbish-removal']],
 'dishwasher-repair': ['Standing water, an interrupted cycle or leaking', 'Tell Ellis the model and what the appliance does when the fault occurs. We assess the appliance and its connections before agreeing repairs. A visible puddle may involve the machine or surrounding plumbing, rather than one assumed part.', 'Repairing the appliance or fitting a replacement', 'Parts availability, condition and the diagnosed fault affect the repair option. A new dishwasher may also need the opening and connections checked. We distinguish appliance work, cabinet alterations and plumbing or electrical changes in the quote.', 'Fault investigation, compatible parts, access, removal and any connection changes affect the repair price.', ['plumbers','cabinet-makers']],
 'removalists': ['Moving household furniture between properties', 'Ellis checks the item list and access at both addresses before agreeing the move. Include stairs, lifts, parking and bulky items. The plan distinguishes transport from packing, disassembly and reassembly so the included help is clear.', 'Preparing furniture for a repair or renovation', 'A room clear-out can be planned around flooring or other work. Tell us what needs moving and where it will be placed. Product-specific assembly and fixing are separately assessed rather than assumed for every item moved.', 'Item quantity, size, travel, stairs or lifts, parking and packing or assembly tasks affect the quote.', ['handymen','floor-sanding']],
 'gas-fitters': ['Replacing a gas appliance or changing its location', 'Tell Ellis the appliance type and the change you want. We arrange the appropriate gas assessment to check the connection and proposed work. Appliance supply, gas fitting and related cabinet or ventilation changes are defined separately.', 'A fault enquiry is different from a suspected gas leak', 'A suspected leak needs urgent safety action, not an ordinary future repair booking. Use the appropriate emergency assistance for immediate danger. Routine gas work follows the required qualified assessment and licensing requirements before the installation or repair is agreed.', 'Appliance type, connection changes, access, testing requirements and associated work affect the gas-fitting quote.', ['plumbers','oven-repair']],
 'glass-glaziers': ['A cracked pane or damaged glass panel', 'Tell Ellis the glass location and whether it is cracked, loose or broken. We assess the panel and frame before agreeing replacement. Height, panel size and the required glass type affect handling; do not remove damaged glass to prepare the enquiry.', 'Glass replacement, mirrors and pet door installations', 'A mirror mounting and a replacement window pane have different fitting requirements. Pet doors in glass are also available, with the panel and product checked for a suitable installation. Some projects require a purpose-made replacement pane instead of cutting the existing one.', 'Glass type and size, frame condition, access, removal and fittings influence the quote.', ['handymen','window-repairs']],
 'handymen': ['A mixed repair list before moving or an inspection', 'Ellis can assess cupboards, doors, wall fittings and furniture tasks together. Identify what should be retained and which repairs need approval. We group compatible work without assuming every item needs replacement or a specialist trade.', 'A small repair or a separate trade project', 'A towel rail fitting, door adjustment and a new power point are not interchangeable jobs. We explain the suitable repair or installation and separate regulated work where required. Your repair list becomes an agreed scope before materials or extra work are approved.', 'Task quantity, fixing surfaces, hardware, materials, access and separate trade work affect the quote; confirm the pricing basis before approval.', ['carpenters','plasterers']],
 'ikea-kitchens': ['An ordered IKEA kitchen ready for assembly and fitting', 'Ellis checks the confirmed plan, supplied cabinets and the room before agreeing installation. Identify missing parts and the appliances to be retained. Kitchen cabinet assembly is distinct from ordinary flat-pack furniture work and needs a complete fitting brief.', 'Preparing the room and arranging connections', 'Walls, floor condition and service positions affect installation. We agree removal and making good where needed. Plumbing, gas and electrical connections are separately identified so cabinetry fitting does not imply that every trade task is included.', 'Cabinet quantity, plan complexity, room preparation, fitting details and separate connections affect the quote.', ['cabinet-makers','plumbers']],
 'oven-repair': ['An oven that will not heat or closes poorly', 'Tell Ellis the model, appliance type and the fault. Heating problems, fan faults and worn seals need different assessment. A door repair and an internal appliance fault are not quoted as the same job simply because both affect cooking.', 'Repair parts or prepare for a replacement appliance', 'Condition and compatible parts influence whether repair is suitable. A replacement also needs the opening and connection requirements checked. Gas or electrical work is handled as the appropriate trade scope rather than an ordinary furniture fitting.', 'Fault diagnosis, parts, appliance access, removal and any connection or cabinet changes affect the quote.', ['electricians','gas-fitters']],
 'pest-control': ['Household pests or signs of recurring activity', 'Tell Ellis where activity appears and what you have noticed. We arrange assessment to identify the appropriate treatment rather than guess the pest from a brief description. Include earlier treatments and any recurring affected areas.', 'Defining treatment and follow-up expectations', 'The plan identifies the pest concern, treatment area and any follow-up included. Tell us about children, pets and sensitive occupants so preparation can be discussed. A household treatment enquiry is not a promise to eliminate every future pest problem.', 'Pest type, affected area, treatment method, access and agreed follow-up affect the price.', ['cleaners','building-inspectors']],
 'rubbish-removal': ['Household clutter or green waste after a clean-up', 'Ellis checks the material types, quantity and collection access before agreeing removal. Describe bulky items and whether the waste is already gathered. A small household load and mixed building waste need different collection arrangements.', 'Declaring materials before loading begins', 'Unknown sheets, chemicals or hazardous residues must be identified rather than included as ordinary rubbish. We confirm suitable handling and disposal arrangements. Labour to dismantle or gather items is separated from transporting an accessible prepared load.', 'Load volume, weight, waste type, gathering work, access and disposal requirements affect the collection quote.', ['garden-clean-up','asbestos-removal']],
 'upholstery-repair': ['A torn seam, worn panel or sagging cushion', 'Ellis assesses the fabric, padding and accessible support before agreeing a repair. Tell us whether you want to retain the original material or change the finish. A local seam repair and replacing a complete covering are different jobs.', 'Repairing seating without hiding frame damage', 'Loose support or a damaged frame may need work beyond new fabric. We distinguish upholstery, cushioning and any furniture repair requirements. Matching an aged material depends on available fabric, so the intended appearance is discussed before approval.', 'Item size, fabric availability, repair area, padding, support work and collection requirements affect the quote.', ['handymen','removalists']]
};
